    "bug": {
      "comments": [
        {
          "author": "lvoytek",
          "author_is_release_team": false,
          "content": "With the release of MySQL 9.7, and the push toward the removal of default-mysql-* packages, MariaDB and MySQL should no longer be considered interchangeable. In order to allow packages depending on one or the other to be installed at the same time, mysql-server and mariadb-server along with their dependencies should also be installable at the same time.\n\nTo do this, mariadb-server will need to move its runtime directory from /run/mysqld to /run/mariadbd and its config directory from /etc/mysql to /etc/mariadb. Likewise, remaining MariaDB symlinks used to achieve compatibility should be moved to the mariadb-compat package. Lastly, both mysql-server and mariadb-server binaries with conflicting names will need to be updated, with alternatives symlinks to point to them.\n\nThis update will make the mysql-common package no longer necessary, as my.cnf alternatives will no longer be needed. Once the removal of default-mysql-* is complete, mysql-defaults can be removed completely.",
          "content_sha": "94bac93ed73b03d35df0d93abd924a576126f2f66e84959d5be9c68cae7b3f14",
          "date_created": "2026-09-16T12:39:31.955554+00:00",
          "index": 0,
          "url": "https://bugs.launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/mysql-9.7/+bug/2167479/comments/0"
        },
        {
          "author": "otto",
          "author_is_release_team": false,
          "content": "Latest 1:11.8.9+ds-3 ships now with https://salsa.debian.org/mariadb-team/mariadb-server/-/merge_requests/178",
          "content_sha": "07c4b43f16d4d49412b6f265c1bb519374628de8308c06d574e0eff6968834c0",
          "date_created": "2026-09-21T01:20:10.182119+00:00",
          "index": 1,
          "url": "https://bugs.launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/mysql-9.7/+bug/2167479/comments/1"
        }
      ],
      "date_created": "2026-09-16T12:39:31.955554+00:00",
      "date_last_message": "2026-09-21T01:20:10.182119+00:00",
      "date_last_updated": "2026-09-25T20:00:20.350280+00:00",
      "description": "Hello Release team,\n\nPlease accept this FFE to update MariaDB and MySQL in stonking to allow the two servers to be co-installed. This allows us to make sure packages depending directly on mariadb-server or mysql-server can be installed and used at the same time, which mitigates issues caused by Debian's move toward removing default-mysql-* packages (https://lists.debian.org/debian-devel/2026/05/msg00161.html).\n\nThe changes required are shown in attached merge proposals. On the mariadb side this includes\n\n- Moving the config directory from /etc/mysql to /etc/mariadb\n- Removing /etc/mysql/my.cnf alternatives use and removing mysql-common dependency\n- Renaming the binaries my_print_defaults, perror, innochecksum, myisam_ftdump, myisamchk, myisamlog and myisampack, adding symlinks with original names to them in mariadb-server-compat\n- Moving remaining mysql compat symlinks to mariadb-server-compat\n- Adding port 3306 backoff to 3307 logic when 3306 is in use\n- Updating package conflicts\n\nOn the mysql side this includes\n\n- Adding port 3306 backoff to 3307 logic when 3306 is in use\n- Updating package conflicts\n\n\nPPA with changes here - https://launchpad.net/~lvoytek/+archive/ubuntu/mariadb-mysql-co-install\n\nAutopkgtests for both packages are passing, including upstream test suite tests, and using the packages from the PPA confirms that mariadb-server and mysql-server can be installed/removed/purged in any combination together on the same system.\n\nNotably the removal of mysql-defaults is not necessary to solve this issue, and we can wait on that till next cycle.\n\n\n[Original info]\n\nWith the release of MySQL 9.7, and the push toward the removal of default-mysql-* packages, MariaDB and MySQL should no longer be considered interchangeable. In order to allow packages depending on one or the other to be installed at the same time, mysql-server and mariadb-server along with their dependencies should also be installable at the same time.\n\nTo do this, mariadb-server will need to move its runtime directory from /run/mysqld to /run/mariadbd and its config directory from /etc/mysql to /etc/mariadb. Likewise, remaining MariaDB symlinks used to achieve compatibility should be moved to the mariadb-compat package. Lastly, both mysql-server and mariadb-server binaries with conflicting names will need to be updated, with alternatives symlinks to point to them.\n\nThis update will make the mysql-common package no longer necessary, as my.cnf alternatives will no longer be needed. Once the removal of default-mysql-* is complete, mysql-defaults can be removed completely.",
      "description_sha": "efc2d9254124a1a5feb5880530cd11ed3283b02a319d3ef8bfc08ad13b7fee26",
